  "name": "track plan: a meet on a crossing loop",
  "covers": [
    "Track plan: a crossing loop meet"
  ],
  "about": "A westbound train takes the single line, the east points and the main road. An eastbound train waits at West Home: the main road is taken, so it waits until the west points are set for the siding, then takes the siding. Arriving in the loop, neither is taken for a train waiting at the signal it came past (Main East, Siding West): only the piece of track it came through says so. Each waits at its own exit, and goes once the points ahead are set for it and the pieces it needs have been clear for 3 seconds. A turnout is locked from the scan after its signal clears for a waiting train, and while a train is short of it or over it.",
